#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# inverse_jacobi_dn

#% text
# `inverse_jacobi_dn(v, m)` gives the `u` with `jacobi_dn(u, m) = v`, the inverse of the Jacobi elliptic function `dn`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The value is the principal branch of DLMF 22.15, real for a real `v` in the range of the function on the real line and `0 <= m < 1`.
#% item
# For a real `m > 1` the value is `inverse_jacobi_cn(v, 1/m)/sqrt(m)` (the reciprocal-modulus transformation, DLMF 22.17), real for a real `v` in the range of the function on the real line.

#% item
# Machine numbers and balls give numerical values; exact arguments stay unevaluated.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
inverse_jacobi_dn(0.9, 0.5)
#% output
#= 0.6887927923955088

#% cell
inverse_jacobi_dn(1.0, 0.5)
#% output
#= 0.0

#% cell
inverse_jacobi_dn(0.85, 0.3)
#% output
#= 1.384095511392369

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# `jacobi_dn` undoes it:

#% cell
jacobi_dn(inverse_jacobi_dn(0.9, 0.4), 0.4)
#% output
#= 0.9

#% text
# The inverse grows to the quarter period `K(m)` at the end of the range:

#% cell
[inverse_jacobi_dn(sqrt(0.5), 0.5), elliptic_k(0.5)]
#% output
#= [1.8540746562279475, 1.8540746773013719]

